This is NOT a signature. ots-5.74.1.plugin was built without a signing
key, so no detached signature exists for it, and the SHA-256 checksum beside it
is the verification available for this release.

This file is plain text on purpose. It stands where a stale signature used to
sit: the alias had kept the last signed release's .asc, which would fail against
this package as a BAD signature and read as if the download had been tampered
with. Refusing to look like a signature is the honest state.

Verify with:
  shasum -a 256 ots.plugin
and compare against ots-5.74.1.plugin.sha256.

Releases up to 5.61.3 ship a real detached signature beside the package.
